        "id": 217828,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-01-02T16:00:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Thanos is obviously not all there, so even if he's smart and powerful enough to get all the Infinity Gems it doesn't mean he's thought a plan like this on such a grand level through. He's called \"The Mad Titan\" in the comics for a reason.</p>\n<p>Also, you must realize his reasoning for killing off half of all life in the universe is WAY different than why he did it in the comics(He was in love with the personification of Death, an actual character in the Marvel Universe, and to test his devotion she charges Thanos to kill of half of all life in the universe). I will agree that it's strange to alter the character's driving motivations and not change their resulting actions to reflect it, though.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:49:49.004Z",
